From 33603dbcf022bf30241967bdcf8438ee397e79b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 03:13:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] chore: re-pin the door daemons + wire agreements to
 upstream HEAD
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Moves door-keeper, door-kit, keeper-wire, door-scout, scout-wire,
door-concierge and concierge-wire forward together to their 2026-08/09
heads. They have to move as a set: door-kit is the client side of all
three wire checks, and its scout client already speaks the four methods
(repos/project/orgOpenWork/orgMergedPrs) that door-scout + scout-wire
added after the old pin — bumping only the keeper trio would turn
scout-wire red. The post-pin fixes this picks up on the keeper edge are
door-kit#32 (drop the redundant `kind` from import-and-push),
door-keeper#32 (re-vendor the client; closes door-keeper#15) and
keeper-wire#3 (the `pr` verb).

Every flake check is green at these revs (deno run of each check
script against the checked-out revs): keeper-wire, scout-wire,
concierge-wire CONFORM; door-kit-mirror byte-identical;
sanctioned-reader-seam, descriptor-honesty, lattice pass.

Lock entries were computed without nix (rev = origin/main, lastModified
= committer timestamp, narHash = NAR sha256 of the tree); the method was
validated by reproducing all nine existing entries bit-for-bit. If a
maintainer prefers, `nix flake lock --update-input <each>` regenerates
the same entries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CVjvRP7P9oSiX3uhjK1xsz
